title: "NEM-Nav: Neuro-Symbolic Episodic Memory for Zero-Shot Object-Goal Navigation"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2024-12-01
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/anonymous/nem-nav"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Anonymous"
    family-names: "Authors"
keywords:
  - object-goal-navigation
  - embodied-ai
  - episodic-memory
  - vision-language
  - neuro-symbolic
abstract: >-
  NEM-Nav is a modular system for zero-shot object-goal navigation that
  augments classical frontier exploration with three inter-operable
  priors -- a FAISS episodic memory of dense observation embeddings, a
  topological semantic graph that compresses repeated experiences, and a
  deterministic structured planner that converts a short goal text into
  a target-room hypothesis. All four signals are linearly combined into
  an interpretable per-cell action score so that every component can be
  ablated cleanly. Evaluation uses a procedurally generated semantic
  apartment testbed with hand-curated room/object ontology,
  partial-observability cone perception, and oracle shortest-path
  supervision for SPL.
